# Firebase web config for the production build (GitHub Pages, kupatakipucl.com).
#
# These values are deliberately committed, and that is safe. Vite inlines every
# VITE_* var into the JS bundle at build time, so all six are already served to
# every visitor as plain text in dist/assets/index-*.js — you can read the API
# key out of the deployed site with view-source. Hiding them here would protect
# nothing.
#
# What actually secures the project is elsewhere, and must stay that way:
#   - firestore.rules / storage.rules / database.rules.json  — who may read and
#     write what. This is the real access control.
#   - Firebase Auth authorized domains — which origins may complete a Google
#     sign-in. Only localhost, kupatakipucl.firebaseapp.com, kupatakipucl.web.app,
#     kupatakipucl.com and www.kupatakipucl.com. Someone who copies this config
#     onto their own host cannot sign anybody in.
#
# The alternative was six GitHub Actions repository variables. Rejected: it moves
# build-critical values out of the repo, where a single typo produces a build
# that succeeds and then cannot reach Firebase at runtime — and a fresh clone
# could no longer produce a working build. deploy.yml asserts these landed in the
# bundle, so that failure mode is caught in CI either way.
#
# .env.local still exists for local dev and still overrides this file. Keep the
# two in sync if the Firebase project is ever changed.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyCRi1SpktpzYKIY7WAGBwBxXNuZWS-qSdU
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=kupatakipucl.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=kupatakipucl
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:626901876973:web:627a00ad9f46fd4c088ce4
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=kupatakipucl.firebasestorage.app
VITE_FIREBASE_DATABASE_URL=https://kupatakipucl-default-rtdb.europe-west1.firebasedatabase.app
